 393| One kilogram of airborne mass adds 1.0 to the score (NR-046).
 399| The score adds three soft constraint penalties to the airborne mass (NR-046):
 400| `f = mass + 5.0 * max(P_score - 5.0, 0)^2 + 20.0 * (2.5 / FoS_min)^2 + 1.0 * (r / (1 - r))^2`
 401| with `r = min(twist_ratio, 1)`, plus the stationarity add-on `10.0 * max(0, swing - 0.20)`.
 403| The over-power charge reads P_score, the end power, against the 5.0 kW ceiling (NR-046).
 404| The utilisation charge reads the window-minimum factor of safety against the 2.5 floor (NR-046).
 405| The twist charge reads the worst segment twist ratio against the crossing limit (NR-046).
 406| The stationarity add-on reads the window swing against 20 per cent (NR-046).
 408| Every charge is continuous. None is step-like (NR-046).
 412| The runner stamps the search cost `1e9` on every non-ok design (NR-046).
