 866| ## 5 Conclusion
 868| The report screened 930 rigid-wing ground-generation rotary kite turbine designs with a tensile rotary power transmission (NR-001).
 869| The campaign scored each design on the ODE path over the measurement window (NR-015).
 870| One fixed power-law generator load and one fixed gate set held for every design (NR-015).
 872| The search found 508 feasible candidates in the searched space (NR-002).
 873| The best performing one had a mean power of 5.309 kW.
 874| Its airborne mass is 25.698 kilograms (NR-008, NR-018).
 875| Its window-minimum factor of safety is 15.0 (NR-009).
 876| All checked TRPT rings and twist segments operate below their failure boundaries at the final operating point (NR-021, NR-022).
 877| The least segment torque margin is 2.03, at S1 (NR-040).
 883| The rapid path awaits its rope-break gate fix (NR-013).
